And it's pretty much insoluble: rank always goes up on wins, and down on 
losses, but since the bot _never_ attacks we have no real way of 
affecting the bot's rank.

OK, that's not exactly true: we could tweak the bot to make it more 
likely to win, but we've chosen a specific values for its stats, a 
specific familiar and specific equipment all for a reason.  The reason 
should be pretty obvious if you look at it.  ;-)

And I can appreciate the annoyance of having to break your hippy stone 
for it, since I have to do that two weeks before the Tournament on my 
account to verify that everything still works.  As Ken pointed out, 
arranging to leave your important stuff in Hangk's is a good idea.  It's 
also a good idea to prep yourself for defense (meat golem, meat locker, 
fences and such); I put about 5k meat into PvP campground furnishings 
before I broke my stone for testing this year.

There's really nothing else we can do, though, since PvP is the only 
mechanism for inter-player conflict in KoL so if we want a system where 
you actually "defeat" The Wizard in KoL it's kinda the only option.

